.Dd $Mdocdate: August 3 2026 $
.Dt RECUEIL 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm recueil
.Nd pair a device with, and enqueue pages to, a self-hosted Recueil archive
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Cm auth
.Fl -url Ar worker-url
.Op Fl -name Ar device-name
.Nm
.Cm enqueue
.Ar url No ...
.Nm
.Op Fl c Ar file | Fl -config Ar file
.Cm server | agent | gc | user | device
.Op Ar ...
.Nm
.Op Fl -help | Fl -version
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is the single binary behind Recueil, a self-hosted personal web archiver.
Most people will only ever need two of its subcommands:
.Cm auth ,
which pairs the machine
.Nm
is running on with your Recueil instance, and
.Cm enqueue ,
which sends a URL to be archived.
.Pp
Everything else the binary can do
.Pq Cm server , Cm agent , Cm gc , Cm user , Cm device
is there to run and administer a Recueil instance itself, rather than to use
one day-to-day, and is only summarized here; see
.Sx ADMINISTRATIVE COMMANDS
below and the full documentation at
.Lk https://recueil.app/docs .
.Pp
Note that
.Nm
is only one of several ways to send a page to Recueil.
The browser extension, the share-sheet Progressive Web App, and the iOS
Shortcut all do the same job as
.Cm enqueue
without needing a terminal; reach for
.Nm
when you want to script it or you're saving links from a machine that
doesn't have the extension installed.
.Sh GETTING STARTED
.Bl -enum
.It
Sign in to your Recueil dashboard and open the
.Em Devices
screen.
Copy the pairing token shown there.
A pairing token identifies your account; it is not itself a password
and is safe to reuse across every device you pair.
.It
Run
.Ic recueil auth --url https://your-worker.example.workers.dev
and paste the pairing token when prompted.
This exchanges it for a device-specific credential and stores that
credential locally; see
.Sx FILES .
.It
Run
.Ic recueil enqueue https://example.com/some-article
to send a page for archiving.
.El
.Pp
Enqueuing a URL does not archive it immediately.
Recueil only captures pages from a real, already logged-in
browser tab rather than fetching them headlessly, so that login walls,
paywalls, and CAPTCHAs don't defeat it.
Concretely, this means the URL sits in your queue until a paired
browser
.Pq the extension's toolbar popup
picks it up, at which point a tab opens for you to confirm the page
loaded correctly.
If you have no paired browser, enqueued URLs will simply wait.
.Sh COMMANDS
.Ss recueil auth
.Nm
.Cm auth
.Fl -url Ar worker-url
.Op Fl -name Ar device-name
.Pp
Pairs the current machine with a Recueil instance, exchanging a pairing
token for a device credential that
.Cm enqueue
.Pq and any other client on this machine
can then use.
.Pp
The pairing token is read from standard input: interactively, with the
terminal's echo disabled, if standard input is a terminal; otherwise as
a single line, which allows scripted use such as
.Ic echo "$TOKEN" | recueil auth --url ... .
.Pp
The arguments are:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl -url Ar worker-url
The address of your Recueil instance's Worker, as given to you by
whoever set it up.
Required.
.It Fl -name Ar device-name
A label for this device, shown later in the dashboard's Devices
screen so you can tell your paired devices apart.
Defaults to the machine's hostname.
.El
.Pp
Running
.Cm auth
again on a machine that is already paired registers it as a new,
additional device rather than replacing the existing pairing; the old
one keeps working until separately revoked from the dashboard.
.Ss recueil enqueue
.Nm
.Cm enqueue
.Ar url No ...
.Pp
Sends one or more URLs to be archived.
Requires that this device has already been paired via
.Cm auth ;
if it hasn't,
.Cm enqueue
fails immediately with a reminder to run
.Cm auth
first.
.Pp
Each argument is enqueued independently: a malformed URL, or a single
failed request, is reported to standard error and does not stop the
remaining URLs from being enqueued.
If any URL failed,
.Nm
exits non-zero once all of them have been attempted; see
.Sx EXIT STATUS .
.Pp
.Sy Example :
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ recueil enqueue https://example.com/article https://example.org/post
enqueued https://example.com/article
enqueued https://example.org/post
.Ed
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/recueil/credentials.json
The device credential written by
.Cm auth
and read by
.Cm enqueue .
Falls back to
.Pa $HOME/.config/recueil/credentials.json
if
.Ev XDG_CONFIG_HOME
is unset.
Deleting this file has the same effect as revoking the device from the
dashboard: this machine can no longer enqueue anything until
.Cm auth
is run again.
.El
.Sh ADMINISTRATIVE COMMANDS
The remaining subcommands run and administer a Recueil instance itself
.Pq the backend server, its background job agent, and account and device management .
They're intended for whoever deployed the instance, are
configured via a TOML file or environment variables rather than
anything
.Cm auth
sets up, and are documented in full, alongside deployment
instructions, at
.Lk https://recueil.app/docs .
In brief:
.Bl -tag -width "recueil device"
.It Ic recueil server
Runs the backend web server and dashboard API.
.It Ic recueil agent
Runs the background jobs that pull queued captures in, generate
thumbnails and readable text, and run optional AI enrichment.
.It Ic recueil gc
Reclaims disk space left behind by deleted pages and captures.
.It Ic recueil user
Creates accounts, resets passwords, and repairs the device-pairing
mirror, directly against the instance's database.
.It Ic recueil device
Lists or revokes a user's paired devices; the operator-side escape
hatch for when the dashboard's own Devices screen isn't reachable.
.El
.Pp
Every administrative subcommand accepts
.Fl c Ar file
.Pq or Fl -config Ar file
to point at a TOML configuration file; see the documentation site for
its contents.
.Cm auth
and
.Cm enqueue
ignore this flag entirely, since they have nothing to do with
configuring an instance.
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Cm enqueue
exits non-zero if any
.Pq not necessarily all
of the given URLs failed to enqueue, after attempting every one of
them.
.Sh SEE ALSO
Full documentation, including deployment and administration:
.Lk https://recueil.app/docs
.Pp
Source code and issue tracker:
.Lk https://github.com/mfinelli/recueil
